age is a simple, modern and secure file encryption tool and format. It
uses small explicit keys, has no configuration options, and composes
with UNIX pipes. Files can be encrypted to X25519 recipients, SSH keys
or passphrases, and plugins extend it to other key types.

This build installs the official statically-linked upstream binary
release; no compiler or Go toolchain is required. Only x86_64 is
supported, since this build only repackages upstream's linux/amd64
tarball.
